#
# Copy this file to .env and fill in the two values. Vite reads it at startup, so
# restart the dev server after a change. .gitignore already covers .env and .env.*,
# and this example is the one exception it lets through.
#
# Both are optional. Without them src/lib/supabase.ts leaves the client null, and
# the app runs anonymous-only: no sign-in button in the header, no cloud
# persistence, everything else works.
#
# The backup workflow takes its database URL, age keys, and separate R2 credentials
# from repository secrets. .github/workflows/backup.yml lists their required scopes.

# The project URL, https://<project-ref>.supabase.co
VITE_SUPABASE_URL=

# The anon (publishable) key. It is public and gated by Row-Level Security, so it
# is meant to ship in the browser bundle. Isolation comes from the database's RLS
# policies, never from hiding this key. The service-role key is a different key
# and does not belong in any VITE_ variable.
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
